1
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:02,790
[sighs]

2
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:06,330
[GRACE] I'm so sick of staying
in this cramped castle.

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,960
I just want to get out
of here so badly

4
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:11,080
and discover a whole new world.

5
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:13,500
That's why I'm going
to the surface.

6
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:15,130
[RIGMOR] The surface?

7
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:18,040
That's right. Where those
creatures called humans live.

8
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:21,080
And up there, they have
much freer lives than we do.

9
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,630
Humans have these strange
legs which they use to walk,

10
00:00:24,710 --> 00:00:27,500
and without them, they
can't even swim on land.

11
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:30,630
Oh wow, but how are
you gonna get there?

12
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:31,630
Hmm.

13
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:34,460
Although, a brand new world?

14
00:00:34,830 --> 00:00:36,790
That sounds just
like a beautiful dream.

15
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:40,420
I really hope I get
to see it as well.

16
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:41,960
To see that world.

17
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,880
To share your dream, Grace.

18
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:47,170
Yeah. Rigmor?

19
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,960
[GRACE] Someday we'll
go to the surface.

20
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,330
I know we will.

21
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:53,040
After all, that's our dream.

22
00:00:53,830 --> 00:00:55,130
[magical sound]

23
00:00:57,630 --> 00:00:58,670
[sighs]

24
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:00,420
[SEA SNAKE] We need to go

25
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:03,250
deeper.

26
00:01:04,630 --> 00:01:06,290
All the way down.

27
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,670
[♪ opening music begins]

28
00:02:34,130 --> 00:02:36,040
[♪ opening music ends]

29
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:40,670
Wake up.

30
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:43,830
[gasps]

31
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:47,790
Come. We don't have time.

32
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:49,830
Follow me.

33
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:54,500
What is this place?

34
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:00,580
This is Lady Grace's
secret room.

35
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:04,330
Is this...?

36
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:06,170
[SEA SNAKE] A magic mirror.

37
00:03:06,830 --> 00:03:09,460
It is useless to me
as I am unable to see,

38
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:12,330
but you should
be able to see it.

39
00:03:13,630 --> 00:03:15,500
Whatever it is you
are longing for,

40
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:17,080
it will show you.

41
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:20,580
[FEMALE] Where are they?

42
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:23,420
Where have Grace and Rigmor
gone to?

43
00:03:24,290 --> 00:03:27,210
Those twins just don't have
a clue that they're royal

44
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,880
princesses and
important to us all.

45
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:31,420
They just don't realize

46
00:03:31,630 --> 00:03:35,000
they must bring light to this
castle as soon as possible.

47
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,250
Especially Grace.

48
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:40,790
She doesn't even have the
decency to listen to me anymore.

49
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:43,170
Only yesterday
she broke into the treasury

50
00:03:43,250 --> 00:03:45,250
and didn't even stop
when I told her.

51
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:47,710
She even ransacked
the forbidden relics.

52
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:50,170
I don't know what
goes on in that mind.

53
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:52,790
Grace is pretty thoughtful
when she can be.

54
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,500
I often wonder if
she's really needed in

55
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,130
this castle in the first place.

56
00:03:57,330 --> 00:03:59,750
[FEMALE] Rowan,
don't be ridiculous.

57
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:02,330
Thinking thoughts like
that will only keep

58
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:04,130
the light at a distance.

59
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:06,420
Rigmor, look!

60
00:04:07,210 --> 00:04:10,210
The 2 big sticks are protruding
out of the storehouse still.

61
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:12,630
This must be what
humans look like.

62
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:16,000
I wonder why this one
has 2 dorsal fins.

63
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:18,630
They can't possibly
swim like that.

64
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:20,000
Do you know?

65
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:21,210
No idea.

66
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:24,540
But looking at these humans,
they seem to be the type

67
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:25,960
who'll try to do anything.

68
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,130
We should be like them,

69
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:30,420
have that same
passion to explore.

70
00:04:31,210 --> 00:04:33,960
So let's get out of this
castle as soon as possible,

71
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,460
and then we can make
our dream come true.

72
00:04:37,330 --> 00:04:38,170
Speaking of,

73
00:04:38,790 --> 00:04:40,500
I found something
that will help us.

74
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:41,880
How interesting!

75
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:43,380
Go on!

76
00:04:43,670 --> 00:04:44,500
Rowan!

77
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:47,210
-Oh, it's you.
-What're you doing here?

78
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,500
Somebody's in a bad mood.

79
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,170
You'll tell that hag
everything, won't you?

80
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:54,630
He wouldn't!
Rowan is on your side.

81
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,920
He shares your concern
for the castle.

82
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:58,130
He won't tell anyone.

83
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,130
[ROWAN] Our castle
is losing its light,

84
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:03,380
and it's growing
colder every day.

85
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,830
It won't survive
much longer like this.

86
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:08,170
That's why I admire you.

87
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:10,170
You're out in the world causing

88
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:12,330
all that chaos for
the sake of the castle.

89
00:05:14,290 --> 00:05:16,500
-You're wrong, though.
-About what?

90
00:05:18,670 --> 00:05:21,750
[GRACE] I don't do it for
the castle. It's because—

91
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,580
It's because I can—

92
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:27,540
I can feel the light and
the dreams of the world.

93
00:05:27,710 --> 00:05:28,830
[magical sound]

94
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:32,290
[♪ soft music]

95
00:05:32,630 --> 00:05:33,460
[gasps]

96
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:34,880
The king is—

97
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,460
[bubbling]

98
00:05:47,170 --> 00:05:48,460
[WOMAN] We must hurry now.

99
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:51,210
The throne cannot
be vacant for long.

100
00:05:51,830 --> 00:05:54,710
We need the long-lost
power of the princess.

101
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:58,670
If things continue like this,
then the castle will—

102
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:02,080
Now the fate of everything
rests on your shoulders.

103
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:05,080
You must find the
light of true love

104
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:07,790
as soon as you possibly can.

105
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:13,630
[GRACE] I'm suffocating here.
That old hag,

106
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:14,750
the castle folk.

107
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,000
They're all forcing this
ridiculous fate on us.

108
00:06:19,330 --> 00:06:20,170
I'm sick of it.

109
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:23,500
We have to get out of this place
as soon as possible.

110
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:25,580
Then we can finally
follow our dreams.

111
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,420
Grace, listen, I think—

112
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,330
[gasps]

113
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:35,790
What is that?

114
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:39,500
This is a potion that can
turn us into humans.

115
00:06:41,330 --> 00:06:42,460
I finally found it.

116
00:06:43,210 --> 00:06:45,420
It was hidden away
deep in the castle.

117
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:46,710
[sighs]

118
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:49,420
This elixir can alter
the very form of life.

119
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,040
If we use it, we can realize our
dream of going to the surface.

120
00:06:54,710 --> 00:06:55,880
Let's go together.

121
00:06:56,710 --> 00:06:58,420
Our dream can finally come true.

122
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:02,040
[sighs]

123
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:06,420
[♪ soft piano music]

124
00:07:09,670 --> 00:07:12,880
Surely not because of that
whole destiny thing.

125
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:17,210
[RIGMOR] That's not it.
The thing is, I've—

126
00:07:18,130 --> 00:07:20,420
fallen in love with him,

127
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:22,040
with Rowan.

128
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:25,830
That's why I've decided,

129
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:28,750
I'll continue to live here
in the castle.

130
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,920
So, was it all a lie?

131
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,040
Was I the only one who thought
we shared the same dream

132
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:39,380
of going to the surface?

133
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
[RIGMOR] No!
No, Grace!

134
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:48,210
I'm leaving.

135
00:07:50,210 --> 00:07:51,040
[gasps]

136
00:07:53,670 --> 00:07:56,000
Just make sure
you don't forget...

137
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,170
your amazing dream.

138
00:07:59,290 --> 00:08:00,790
The light you seek up there,

139
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:02,630
it's beautiful.

140
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:06,580
[GRACE] I know.
But now...

141
00:08:07,750 --> 00:08:09,880
it's my dream and mine alone.

142
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:12,540
[♪ somber piano music]

143
00:08:27,250 --> 00:08:30,880
The question is...
where should I go now?

144
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:36,080
[♪ somber music continues]

145
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:40,710
[LISA] Father,
what should I do?

146
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:45,500
Living on the land has
wounded Lara's heart so deeply.

147
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,790
I can't help but think,

148
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:50,170
if only the witch
hadn't given Lara legs.

149
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,000
My child,

150
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:55,250
Lara must come to
terms with her fate.

151
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,210
[♪ gentle piano music]

152
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:11,380
[footsteps]

153
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:23,540
[magical sound]

154
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:27,250
Beautiful.

155
00:09:30,130 --> 00:09:32,170
Rowan, it's you.

156
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:33,830
I love you.

157
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:35,290
[magical sound]

158
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,170
[magical sound]

159
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:43,000
[everybody gasping]

160
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:45,540
-It's incredible!
-Light!

161
00:09:45,630 --> 00:09:46,960
[mermaids chattering]

162
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,000
It's the light
from the princess!

163
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:57,000
It's Lady Rigmor
and Lord Rowan!

164
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:59,210
They've united in true love!

165
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:03,080
[MALE] It's wonderful!
A new princess has been born!

166
00:10:05,710 --> 00:10:06,540
[ROWAN] My love,

167
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:10,040
you are to me like
a flower in bloom.

168
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,880
I want to always bring you joy.

169
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:15,080
[RIGMOR] My dear one,

170
00:10:16,170 --> 00:10:18,000
I'm with you for a reason.

171
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:21,630
I once was searching
for a dazzling light.

172
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:23,080
[magical sound]

173
00:10:23,670 --> 00:10:26,710
[RIGMOR] Now I feel that light
deep within my heart.

174
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:28,960
It's the light of love.

175
00:10:31,330 --> 00:10:33,170
I feel that light in
my heart as well.

176
00:10:33,790 --> 00:10:36,170
Now that light fills
every corner of the castle,

177
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,880
and new princesses
are on their way.

178
00:10:40,670 --> 00:10:42,250
Look at this wonderful sight.

179
00:10:42,670 --> 00:10:45,040
[RIGMOR] Yes, it's
truly beautiful.

180
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:48,540
I hope this light will continue
to fill the world forever,

181
00:10:49,290 --> 00:10:51,790
[RIGMOR] For all mermaids
everywhere.

182
00:10:54,130 --> 00:10:56,170
[ROWAN] Yes. For all mermaids.

183
00:10:58,170 --> 00:11:00,460
Lady Rigmor believes that
Lady Grace left because

184
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:02,250
of her, that it was her fault.

185
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:05,380
They were inseparable twins
for years.

186
00:11:05,630 --> 00:11:07,130
It must be painful for her,

187
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:10,670
but from now on, they will
never be able to meet again.

188
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:14,790
We are beings who live our
lives purely by the light,

189
00:11:15,210 --> 00:11:19,380
and humans are beings who
live only by words alone.

190
00:11:20,330 --> 00:11:23,670
Humans will always reject
that which cannot be spoken.

191
00:11:24,630 --> 00:11:27,420
There is but only one fate
that awaits a mermaid

192
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,040
who ascends to the human world.

193
00:11:30,330 --> 00:11:32,540
[♪ dramatic music]

194
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,380
[magical sound]

195
00:11:37,790 --> 00:11:40,000
[MALE] What is that form?
What are you?

196
00:11:42,420 --> 00:11:46,290
Can't be. Were you...
deceiving me?

197
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:49,540
All along, you were hiding
your true hideous form!

198
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:51,710
-No, I wasn't deceiving—
-Shut up!

199
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:55,040
Monsters like mermaids
use sweet words

200
00:11:55,250 --> 00:11:56,670
and lure us into their traps.

201
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:57,920
No!

202
00:11:58,330 --> 00:12:00,880
No, you're wrong!
I truly love you!

203
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,580
How can you? You don't
even have a human heart.

204
00:12:03,710 --> 00:12:05,250
[GRACE] No, you're wrong.

205
00:12:05,710 --> 00:12:07,500
I am human!

206
00:12:07,710 --> 00:12:08,540
You're a liar!

207
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,250
You use human words,

208
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:12,710
but you're a hideous monster.

209
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,000
[♪ dramatic music ends]

210
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:15,750
[beat]

211
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:22,920
[gasps]

212
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,130
[♪ dramatic music]

213
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:26,750
Grace.

214
00:12:28,250 --> 00:12:30,710
[distant voices calling]

215
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:35,500
[Grace gasping and sobbing]

216
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,250
This can't... be real.

217
00:12:43,670 --> 00:12:44,500
What have I—

218
00:12:46,250 --> 00:12:47,080
Please, no.

219
00:12:48,380 --> 00:12:50,040
What on earth have I just done?

220
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:53,040
[cracking]

221
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:55,170
[♪ dramatic music]

222
00:12:56,130 --> 00:12:57,380
[magical sound]

223
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,000
[♪ dramatic music]

224
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,210
[MAN 1] Hey, I found them!

225
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:16,330
[MAN 2] What is this monster?
[MAN 1] It's something evil!

226
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:18,080
-Kill it!
-Go forward!

227
00:13:18,210 --> 00:13:19,170
[all clamoring]

228
00:13:19,250 --> 00:13:20,500
-Get it!
-Get out of here!

229
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:22,960
[all shouting]

230
00:13:25,130 --> 00:13:27,210
[ALL SHOUTING] Come on, get it!

231
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:29,540
[♪ dramatic music]

232
00:13:36,710 --> 00:13:38,920
[splash]

233
00:13:40,710 --> 00:13:43,710
[♪ dramatic music continues]

234
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:47,830
[GRACE] Rigmor...
is this a dream?

235
00:13:48,630 --> 00:13:50,540
[RIGMOR] No, it's not a dream.

236
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:54,420
I heard the voice of your
heart within my own.

237
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:57,830
And I followed the light
of the ring to find you.

238
00:13:59,250 --> 00:14:02,130
[GRACE] Oh, sister...
I'm such...

239
00:14:05,630 --> 00:14:07,580
[Grace sobbing]

240
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:08,790
I...

241
00:14:12,290 --> 00:14:15,000
-I'm such an idiot.
-[RIGMOR] Grace...

242
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,880
I am also an idiot.

243
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:21,130
I just I came out here

244
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,080
all by myself

245
00:14:24,210 --> 00:14:25,830
without even thinking about it.

246
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:29,170
[GRACE] It was
an impossible dream.

247
00:14:29,710 --> 00:14:31,500
Everything I did to come here,

248
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:34,170
in the end it didn't
mean a thing!

249
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,330
[RIGMOR] No.

250
00:14:37,330 --> 00:14:40,710
It did and still does mean
something, because in my

251
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:43,790
eyes I can still see your
beautiful, beautiful dream,

252
00:14:44,790 --> 00:14:46,130
and it doesn't matter.

253
00:14:47,330 --> 00:14:50,250
Whether it's on land or at sea,

254
00:14:51,130 --> 00:14:54,710
it doesn't matter who,
and it doesn't matter why.

255
00:14:55,540 --> 00:14:57,330
As long as we can live for love,

256
00:14:57,460 --> 00:15:00,460
there will always be
light in any place.

257
00:15:01,250 --> 00:15:03,420
It will never fade.

258
00:15:06,830 --> 00:15:07,670
That is...

259
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:10,250
our dream.

260
00:15:12,750 --> 00:15:15,170
[♪ solemn music]

261
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,920
[ROWAN] I will never
forget that sight.

262
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,540
Because of my
loathing for the witch,

263
00:15:41,250 --> 00:15:45,460
along with my immense hatred
toward those murderous humans,

264
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,710
I established a new rule,

265
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:53,290
and that was to never
approach humans ever again.

266
00:15:54,130 --> 00:15:57,540
I strictly enforced it, and
I banished the witch.

267
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:01,080
If she never had the longing
for the surface world,

268
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:03,750
then this tragedy could
have been avoided.

269
00:16:04,210 --> 00:16:05,040
Therefore,

270
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:08,170
I must rid you of
the same chains

271
00:16:08,290 --> 00:16:10,880
that are bound to your
heart and won't let go.

272
00:16:11,290 --> 00:16:13,710
That is the rule for
those who live as mermaids.

273
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:15,920
Lara!
[gasps]

274
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:18,250
[gasps]

275
00:16:19,710 --> 00:16:21,040
[MALE] Do not look away.

276
00:16:21,750 --> 00:16:25,210
This mirror will test the
very heart of the beholder.

277
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:30,170
Watch it through everything
to the very end.

278
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,420
If only the witch would
just disappear forever.

279
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:38,750
[MERMAID 1] But now a new
princess has arrived.

280
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,580
She will serve Lord Rowan.

281
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,460
Another new princess born.

282
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:44,290
She'll bring the light
to the castle.

283
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,380
[mermaids chattering]

284
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,670
Welcome the arrival of my
sister, hereafter known as Lara.

285
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:50,710
[LARA] I wonder if—

286
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:55,080
Well, are humans really such
hideous creatures after all?

287
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:03,330
[SNAKE] Lady Grace,
that potion is—

288
00:17:03,630 --> 00:17:04,460
Is what?

289
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:07,210
I just want to see it,
that's all.

290
00:17:07,790 --> 00:17:11,710
I want to see the ending
of that foolish mermaid's story.

291
00:17:12,250 --> 00:17:13,540
[magical sound]

292
00:17:24,250 --> 00:17:26,540
[glass shattering]

293
00:17:33,330 --> 00:17:34,170
Lady Grace.

294
00:17:36,170 --> 00:17:37,000
Why?

295
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:42,960
-Hey!
-Ma'am.

296
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:46,460
Go to the surface immediately
and gather the foam.

297
00:17:47,670 --> 00:17:48,500
Foam?

298
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:50,920
Not a single drop
should be left behind.

299
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,500
Make sure you gather all of it.

300
00:17:53,330 --> 00:17:56,380
[GRACE] Lara, how did
you do it?

301
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:58,670
You protected those you loved,

302
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:00,710
even at the cost
of your own life.

303
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:03,460
You were able to
resist that blade

304
00:18:03,670 --> 00:18:06,130
which sought revenge
for your wounded heart.

305
00:18:07,290 --> 00:18:08,130
Why?

306
00:18:09,250 --> 00:18:12,130
Compared to me,
who killed those I loved

307
00:18:12,380 --> 00:18:13,750
with my own tears.

308
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:17,290
What exactly makes
you so different?

309
00:18:19,170 --> 00:18:20,000
[sighs]

310
00:18:23,630 --> 00:18:25,250
[magical sound]

311
00:18:28,670 --> 00:18:30,380
If only I could live for love.

312
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:32,580
That would be the
most wonderful feeling.

313
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:34,710
[magical sound]

314
00:18:35,130 --> 00:18:35,960
Grace.

315
00:18:41,330 --> 00:18:42,630
[GRACE] No, not yet.

316
00:18:43,210 --> 00:18:44,500
I won't let it end yet.

317
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:45,710
I won't.

318
00:18:46,750 --> 00:18:48,710
I'm going to see
the rest of this story,

319
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,290
see how it plays out.

320
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:52,750
No matter what.

321
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:54,960
-Witch.
-Um.

322
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:58,670
So Lara really is
coming back to life?

323
00:18:59,330 --> 00:19:00,170
Is that true?

324
00:19:01,250 --> 00:19:04,880
Of course, because I drained all
of the light from her father,

325
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:06,830
and gave it to her.

326
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:09,330
Very well.

327
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:13,630
As long as I have
Lara, as long...

328
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:17,130
as her princess's
light can still shine,

329
00:19:17,710 --> 00:19:20,500
that power could become
so intense that it sees

330
00:19:20,630 --> 00:19:22,830
the destruction of mankind.

331
00:19:23,670 --> 00:19:24,500
[thump]

332
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:26,920
You're using too much power.

333
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:29,460
You shouldn't put so many
mermaids to sleep.

334
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:30,630
It's too much.

335
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:33,670
[GRACE] Eventually,
Lara will awaken

336
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,920
and she will face a new trial.

337
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:40,580
So if I don't put Rowan
and the others to sleep,

338
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,630
they will get in her way.

339
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:45,420
[SNAKE] But still, this
power is too strong.

340
00:19:46,330 --> 00:19:49,250
[GRACE] In that case, I'll
simply cast aside this body.

341
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:51,670
If I inhabit a little vessel,

342
00:19:52,170 --> 00:19:54,210
then my power will
last a little longer.

343
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:56,750
I will keep waiting for her.

344
00:19:57,290 --> 00:19:59,920
I will be there when Lara
wakes up once more.

345
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,830
[grunts]

346
00:20:10,670 --> 00:20:12,670
[♪ dramatic music ends]

347
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:16,420
[♪ solemn music]

348
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:19,290
[GRACE] Hurry!

349
00:20:20,630 --> 00:20:22,540
Hurry and be reborn, Lara.

350
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:25,460
I still want to see it.

351
00:20:26,710 --> 00:20:27,880
Your whole story.

352
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:32,830
Because you— you are the very
last remaining light to me.

353
00:20:33,630 --> 00:20:34,540
For even I,

354
00:20:34,630 --> 00:20:37,750
who lost my light after taking
the life of my beloved,

355
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,130
even I can see it.

356
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,460
The one and only light.

357
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:46,210
You, out of everyone, possess
a pure and true heart.

358
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:47,580
You are the one.

359
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,500
who can make it happen.

360
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:52,830
The dream of the surface.

361
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:55,420
Otherwise,

362
00:20:56,540 --> 00:20:58,630
if there's no light
on the land,

363
00:21:00,210 --> 00:21:01,040
then why?

364
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:05,330
Why have I ended up here?

365
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:07,830
[gasps]

366
00:21:13,670 --> 00:21:14,540
[MARI] It moved.

367
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:16,710
Oh...

368
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:18,920
It's not dead,

369
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,380
but it closed its eyes again.
Not good.

370
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:27,540
-Are you dead?
-Do shut up.

371
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:28,920
Uh.

372
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:31,580
At least let me have some
peace at the end.

373
00:21:31,750 --> 00:21:32,580
Huh?

374
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:34,330
Did it just talk?

375
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:37,250
Hmm?

376
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:40,830
Hey, stop it! What do you think
you're doing?

377
00:21:42,380 --> 00:21:44,880
You little brat.
Put me down right now!

378
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:49,290
You're a bit rude for a fish.
But you'll be okay.

379
00:21:50,540 --> 00:21:52,920
You don't have to die,
not just yet.

380
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:56,580
[♪ closing music begins]

381
00:22:50,580 --> 00:22:52,330
I see it.
[glass shattering]

382
00:22:53,830 --> 00:22:54,790
I see the light.

383
00:22:55,130 --> 00:22:55,960
[gasps]

384
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:58,040
I can always see it.

385
00:22:59,710 --> 00:23:01,290
Such a beautiful light.

386
00:23:03,630 --> 00:23:05,500
[Mari cries]
[GRACE] I can still see.

387
00:23:07,210 --> 00:23:08,040
Light.

388
00:23:09,750 --> 00:23:10,580
The dream.

389
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:12,880
I know.

390
00:23:15,710 --> 00:23:16,670
It's still there.

391
00:23:17,670 --> 00:23:19,750
[Mari sobs]

392
00:23:20,630 --> 00:23:23,500
[Mari cries]

393
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:26,790
[♪ closing music ends]

394
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:29,790
[GRACE] Lara.

395
00:23:31,630 --> 00:23:32,460
Mari.

396
00:23:32,710 --> 00:23:33,580
[gasps]

397
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:38,750
Don't live by rules.

398
00:23:39,630 --> 00:23:41,040
Live for love.

399
00:23:42,330 --> 00:23:43,290
[glass shatters]

400
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:48,040
[dramatic sound]

401
00:23:58,460 --> 00:24:00,000
TO BE CONTINUED
